      "message": "Could we honour timeout here instead of discarding it? libspdm calculates the receive timeout but relies on this callback to enforce it. The blocking recv()/recvfrom() calls can otherwise wait indefinitely if the responder does not reply, leaving spdmd unable to process further D-Bus requests.\n\nOne option is to set SO_RCVTIMEO before receiving and return LIBSPDM_STATUS_RECEIVE_FAIL on EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK. Zero timeout needs nonblocking handling, since a zero socket timeout disables the timeout. Please account for both the peek and the subsequent read. The send path at L308 similarly ignores its timeout and could use SO_SNDTIMEO.\n\nHappy to provide a follow-up patch if preferred.",
